{"title":"2004 OIM Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_OIM_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> of points in the plane, a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in the plane is said to be a \"<i>cut point</i>\" of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> if there are four different points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299ddf7c0f03ea46bf09f81f93adeea0756aa15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> such that the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are different and intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Given a finite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cce761941ab4b57ae903d05b8fa0568ebbdd98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> of points in the plane, a sequence of sets is constructed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/4/004b6364f20475a1552fd4609ceff639b7534b24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, A_2, A_3, \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /> as follows: for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/d/b3d2402f8a0caa19a501610e4d57f728922aeadd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f965eb64a47d93b2f0a7ae353e1e1595215fb02d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{j+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"39\" height=\"19\" /> is the union of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6edb286660f22d694ff4152ede3c948864cbb99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> with the set of all <i>cut points</i> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6edb286660f22d694ff4152ede3c948864cbb99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />.  Show that if the union of all the sets of the sequence is a finite set, then for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/1/e917cc69cebd38d3d32b6957b20f692588cb2e2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/96297b076158f0f8a1519d0b5956c6899eec08c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_j = A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"68\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_OIM_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2004_OIM_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_OIM_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=OIM_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"OIM Problems and Solutions\">OIM Problems and Solutions</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017204016\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.020 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 101/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 423/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2968/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.546      1 Template:Solution\n100.00%    7.546      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26335:|#|:idhash:canonical and timesta